/* -------------------------------------------------------------------
 * random_2k -- FF_1p95V_n40C
 * AUTO-GENERATED by scripts/rom_char/gen_rom_lib.py -- DO NOT EDIT
 *
 * The OpenRAM ROM compiler does not write a .lib; this file was built
 * from the LEF pins plus the circuit structure extracted from random_2k.sp.
 *
 * Model: precharged NAND-style (series chain) ROM, NO output latch.
 *   clk0 = 0 -> bitlines precharge (dout0 all ones)
 *   clk0 = 1 -> evaluate; the selected cells discharge the bitline
 *   through the series chain;
 *   dout0 valid 1.950 ns later
 *   dout0 becomes INVALID when clk0 falls. The consumer must either
 *   sample on clk0's falling edge, or drive the macro with an inverted
 *   clock (clk0 = ~clk) and capture on the system clock's rising edge.
 *   WARNING: that invalidation is NOT in the Liberty data (no
 *   --t-invalid given). STA will then assume dout0 holds until the
 *   next capture edge and report a FALSE PASS. Pass --t-invalid,
 *   i.e. run through regen_rom_libs.sh.
 *
 * SOURCE: access/t_pre come from ngspice measurements on an isolated column
 * -- THIS corner (FF_1p95V_n40C) was simulated separately with its own
 * sky130 model files (tt/ss/ff); no fixed scaling factor was used.
 * Measurement showed that this matters: the old SS x1.85 assumption was
 * 33% optimistic against the x2.76 that was actually measured.
 * Without --access/--t-pre this script falls back to analytic defaults
 * (based on a wrong NOR model) -- for sign-off ALWAYS call it with
 * measured values, i.e. through regen_rom_libs.sh.
 *
 * WARNING: access covers only the bitline term. clk0 ->
 * precharge/wordline and bitline -> dout0 (inverter + mux + output
 * buffer) are MISSING. Pass the measured values with --t-front /
 * --backend-ns (scripts/rom_char/gen_backend_delay_tb.py).
 *
 * WARNING: HOLD IS AN ANALYTIC GUESS -- 2.1000 ns on every input,
 * from the BASE table in gen_rom_lib.py, not from any measurement.
 * It is a LEFTOVER DEFAULT, roughly 5x shorter than the window the
 * macro really needs, and a hold that is too short is the unsafe
 * direction: STA will pass a design that loses its read. The value
 * is only reachable when --backend-ns is absent, because the rule
 * that replaces it (hold = the full access window) cannot be formed
 * without the back-end term. Pass --backend-ns, or better run
 * scripts/rom_char/regen_rom_libs.sh, which refuses to build a
 * .lib with a term missing.
 *
 * INPUT PIN CAPACITANCES ARE ANALYTIC, NOT MEASURED. They come
 * from gate widths in the netlist (PIN_CAP in gen_rom_lib.py) and
 * one value covers every address bit, which the extraction says
 * cannot be right -- the wire load alone varies several-fold
 * across the bus. Run run_pin_cap.sh and pass --pin-cap.
 *
 * WARNING: no retain_rise/retain_fall -- this file carries LATE
 * data only (worst column). Nothing bounds how SOON dout0 can
 * move, so a hold check against the capture flop cannot fail.
 * Run scripts/rom_char/run_early_path.sh and pass --retain-ns.
 * WARNING: rise/fall_transition NOT MEASURED (fixed guess) --
 * measurement showed that guess was 30-300x too low.
 *
 * WARNING: cell_leakage_power covers the CELL ARRAY ONLY. The
 * clock driver, control NAND, precharge driver, address buffers,
 * row and column decoders, the wordline drivers and the whole read
 * back end (bitline inverters, column mux, output buffers) are
 * scored as ZERO. Run scripts/rom_char/run_periphery_leak.sh and
 * pass --leakage-idle-mw.
 * ----------------------------------------------------------------- */
library (random_2k_FF_1p95V_n40C) {
    delay_model : "table_lookup";
    time_unit : "1ns";
    voltage_unit : "1V";
    current_unit : "1mA";
    resistance_unit : "1kohm";
    capacitive_load_unit(1, pF);
